      "message": "this trick looks a bit hacky to me. If you need grouping, I suggest we use `itertools::group_by` which can group iterators. So `append_service_uuids` could look like:\n\n```\n    fn append_service_uuids(dest: \u0026mut Vec\u003cu8\u003e, uuids: \u0026Vec\u003cUuid\u003e) {\n        for (ad_type, uuids) in uuids\n            .iter()\n            .map(|uuid| UuidHelper::get_shortest_slice(\u0026uuid.uu))\n            .group_by(|uuid| match uuid.len() {\n                2 \u003d\u003e COMPLETE_LIST_16_BIT_SERVICE_UUIDS,\n                4 \u003d\u003e COMPLETE_LIST_32_BIT_SERVICE_UUIDS,\n                16 \u003d\u003e COMPLETE_LIST_128_BIT_SERVICE_UUIDS,\n                _ \u003d\u003e INVALID,\n            })\n            .into_iter()\n        {\n            Self::append_uuids(dest, ad_type, uuids.collect());\n        }\n    }\n\n```\n\nAnd `append_adv_bytes` could look like:\n```\n    fn append_uuids(dest: \u0026mut Vec\u003cu8\u003e, ad_type: u8, uuids: Vec\u003c\u0026[u8]\u003e) {\n        // construct reversed bytes here\n        AdvertiseData::append_adv_data(dest, ad_type, reversed_bytes);\n    }\n```",
