      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T03:06:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The point of this function is to group UUIDS in a compact form.\nUsing group_by() in this way would generates interleaves UUIDs group, for example, [(16_BIT, [id0]), (128_BIT, [id1]), (16_BIT, [id2]). \n\nWhat we expect is: [(16_BIT, [id0, id2]), (32_BIT, [id1])].\nI would like to keep the current implementation as the explicit loop is more intuitive for complicated situations.",
      "parentUuid": "a31bad03_903a74e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 216,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 218,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "3fd52db038d94e53a56a837ef3f34ccb3eb1d5d7",
