      "writtenOn": "2022-10-11T22:08:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "looking at how this was used, I think my recommendation wasn\u0027t optimal since this is returning concrete copied data. If this is how it\u0027s used, it would be more optimal if this returns only a slice so that no data is copied until it really needs to be copied. Something like:\n\n```\n    pub fn get_shortest_slice(uuid: \u0026Uuid128Bit) -\u003e \u0026[u8] {\n        if UuidHelper::in_16bit_uuid_range(uuid) {\n            return \u0026uuid[2..4];\n        } else if UuidHelper::in_32bit_uuid_range(uuid) {\n            return \u0026uuid[0..4];\n        } else {\n            return \u0026uuid[..];\n        }\n    }\n```",
